  <section class="block" id="agents">
    <div class="wrap agent">
      <div>
        <h2>Your coding agent can set it up for you.</h2>
        <p class="intro" style="margin-bottom:24px">Fauxfield ships an MCP server. Claude Code, Codex, and Cursor can create routes from your OpenAPI file or from the page they are building, start the server, and check the traffic. You watch the changes appear in the app as they happen.</p>
        <div class="panel"><div class="bar">One command adds it to your project</div>
<pre><span class="c">$</span> fauxfield agents init --claude
<span class="c">  wrote .mcp.json and a section in AGENTS.md</span></pre></div>
        <p class="demo-note">Prefer shell? Every MCP tool has a CLI twin with <code>--json</code> output.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="panel">
        <div class="bar">Claude Code</div>
        <div class="transcript">
          <div class="who">You</div>
          <div>The billing page needs invoices with paid, overdue, and void states. Mock it and start it.</div>
          <div class="who">Claude</div>
          <div class="tool">fauxfield · upsert_dataset  invoices (24 rows, seeded)</div>
          <div class="tool">fauxfield · upsert_route  GET /invoices  rules: ?status=</div>
          <div class="tool">fauxfield · start_server  billing :3004</div>
          <div class="tool">fauxfield · send_test_request  GET /invoices?status=overdue</div>
          <div class="res">200  6 items  41 ms</div>
          <div style="margin-top:8px">Billing mock is running on :3004 with a CRUD route for invoices and a filtered list. I pointed <span class="mono">VITE_API_URL</span> at it.</div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="block" id="compare">
    <div class="wrap">
      <h2>How it compares.</h2>
      <p class="intro">Each of these tools is good at something. Here is where Fauxfield fits, including where it does not.</p>
      <div class="cmp-wrap">
        <table class="cmp">
          <thead><tr><th scope="col"></th><th scope="col" class="us">Fauxfield</th><th scope="col">Mockoon</th><th scope="col">WireMock</th><th scope="col">Prism</th><th scope="col">json-server</th></tr></thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr><th scope="row">Desktop app</th><td class="us y">Native, GPU</td><td class="y">Electron</td><td class="p">Cloud UI only</td><td class="x">No</td><td class="x">No</td></tr>
            <tr><th scope="row">Headless runner for CI</th><td class="us y">Same binary</td><td class="y">Separate CLI</td><td class="y">Yes</td><td class="y">Yes</td><td class="y">Yes</td></tr>
            <tr><th scope="row">Mocks stored as reviewable files</th><td class="us y">TOML per server</td><td class="p">One JSON file</td><td class="y">JSON mappings</td><td class="y">Your OpenAPI</td><td class="y">One JSON file</td></tr>
            <tr><th scope="row">Conditional responses</th><td class="us y">Yes</td><td class="y">Yes</td><td class="y">Yes</td><td class="p">By example name</td><td class="x">No</td></tr>
            <tr><th scope="row">Stateful CRUD</th><td class="us y">Yes</td><td class="y">Yes</td><td class="p">Via scenarios</td><td class="x">No</td><td class="y">Yes</td></tr>
            <tr><th scope="row">Record and replay</th><td class="us y">Yes</td><td class="y">Yes</td><td class="y">Yes</td><td class="x">No</td><td class="x">No</td></tr>
            <tr><th scope="row">Built-in MCP server for agents</th><td class="us y">Yes</td><td class="x">No</td><td class="x">No</td><td class="x">No</td><td class="x">No</td></tr>
            <tr><th scope="row">Validates traffic against an OpenAPI contract</th><td class="us x">Not in v1.0</td><td class="x">No</td><td class="p">Extension</td><td class="y">Yes</td><td class="x">No</td></tr>
            <tr><th scope="row">Team cloud sync and hosted mocks</th><td class="us x">No<small>By design: local-first</small></td><td class="y">Paid plan</td><td class="y">Paid plan</td><td class="x">No</td><td class="x">No</td></tr>
            <tr><th scope="row">JVM test-library integration</th><td class="us x">No</td><td class="x">No</td><td class="y">JUnit, Spring</td><td class="x">No</td><td class="x">No</td></tr>
            <tr><th scope="row">Years in production, ecosystem size</th><td class="us x">New</td><td class="y">Large</td><td class="y">Very large</td><td class="y">Large</td><td class="y">Very large</td></tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
      <p class="honest">If you need hosted mocks for a distributed team or deep JVM test integration, Mockoon Cloud or WireMock will serve you better today. If you want contract validation of live traffic, use Prism alongside Fauxfield.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="block" id="install">
